<% title "Cohorts (Fuime)" %>

<%# FUIME: where one person vouches for a group in advance.

    See Fuime::Cohort and CreateFuimeCohorts. The short version of why this is
    not a bypass: the decision still happens and a named human still makes it —
    once, ahead of time, with more information than a queue would ever have given
    them — instead of fifty times under time pressure during an event, which is
    how you get a signed record of a judgement nobody made. %>

<h1>Cohorts</h1>

<p class="muted">
  A cohort is a group you vouch for in advance. Founders who enter its code get
  their application approved, their business created and their operator vetting
  recorded automatically — each one attributed to you, with your stated reason.
</p>

<%# The scope of what a code does and does not buy, said plainly on the page
    where somebody creates one. A person about to vouch for fifty strangers
    should not have to read a service object to find out what they are agreeing
    to — and the second half is the part that is easy to assume wrongly. %>
<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">What a code does</h2>
  <p class="mb0"><strong>It does:</strong> approve the application, create the
    business, and record operator vetting as approved — in your name, with your
    reason attached to every one.</p>
  <p class="mb0 mt1"><strong>It does not:</strong> exempt anybody from the rules.
    The services-only scope and the operator age floor still apply and can still
    refuse a venture. It also never stands in for a parent — under
    merchant-of-record a guardian is required before any money is paid out, and
    a cohort cannot change that.</p>
</div>

<%# ── Live and past cohorts ─────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Cohorts</h2>

  <% if @cohorts.any? %>
    <table class="w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Code</th>
          <th>Founders</th>
          <th>Status</th>
          <th>Created by</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @cohorts.each do |cohort| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to cohort.name, cohort_admin_index_path(cohort) %></td>
            <td><code><%= cohort.code %></code></td>
            <td><%= cohort.member_count %> / <%= cohort.max_members %></td>
            <td>
              <%# The reason it is not admitting, not just that it is not. This is
                  the cell somebody reads at 9am on the day the code stops
                  working. %>
              <% if cohort.admitting? %>
                <span class="success">Admitting</span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="muted"><%= cohort.admission_blocker %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td class="muted"><%= cohort.created_by.name %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">None yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# ── Creating one ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

<div class="card">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">New cohort</h2>

  <%= form_with model: @cohort, url: cohort_create_admin_index_path, method: :post, local: true do |form| %>
    <% if @cohort.errors.any? %>
      <div class="error mb2">
        <ul class="mb0">
          <% @cohort.errors.full_messages.each do |message| %>
            <li><%= message %></li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :name, "What's the event or group called?" %>
      <%= form.text_field :name, placeholder: "Founders Weekend, August 2026",
                          maxlength: Fuime::Cohort::MAX_NAME_LENGTH, required: true %>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :code, "The code founders will type" %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-0">
        Letters and numbers only — it gets read aloud and typed by everyone at
        once, so no spaces or dashes.
      </p>
      <%= form.text_field :code, placeholder: "FOUNDERS26",
                          maxlength: Fuime::Cohort::MAX_CODE_LENGTH,
                          autocapitalize: "characters", autocomplete: "off", required: true %>
    </div>

    <%# Required, and the reason it is required is the whole design. This
        sentence is copied verbatim into every vetting note the cohort produces,
        so it has to be something the author is willing to have attached to fifty
        approvals with their name on them. %>
    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :rationale, "Why can you vouch for these founders?" %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-0">
        This is recorded on every business the code admits, next to your name.
        Say what you actually know — "I'm running this event and I know everyone
        attending" is a real answer.
      </p>
      <%= form.text_area :rationale, rows: 3, required: true %>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :expires_at, "The code stops working at" %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-0">
        A code with no end date is a permanent way around vetting for anyone who
        gets hold of it. Set it to just after your event.
      </p>
      <%= form.datetime_field :expires_at, required: true %>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :max_members, "Most founders it will admit" %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-0">
        What turns a leaked code into a bounded problem. A little above your
        actual headcount.
      </p>
      <%= form.number_field :max_members, min: 1, required: true %>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :risk_level, "Risk level for these businesses" %>
      <%= form.select :risk_level,
                      options_for_select(Event.risk_levels.keys.map { |r| [r.humanize, r] },
                                         @cohort.risk_level) %>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :auto_approve do %>
        <%= form.check_box :auto_approve %>
        Set businesses up automatically
      <% end %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-0">
        Off makes this a label you can watch without it admitting anybody — the
        three gates stay manual.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%= form.submit "Create cohort" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
